Every Q4_K mat-vec formulation compiles into one llama-server executable and GGML_VK_Q4K_VARIANT
picks the pipeline at creation time, so an A/B arm changes the module the device compiles and
leaves the load, the shader compiler, the pipeline cache, the build flags, and the executable
digest exactly where they were. The candidate dimension of a served comparison then holds one
term rather than five, and a rate difference between two arms of one process is attributable to
the kernel that ran.

mul_mat_vec_q4_k.comp carries the three formulations under Q4K_VARIANT: 0 is the post-E4
control, 1 adds the four-byte-aligned scale read, and 2 adds the bottom-tested superblock loop
on top of it. 2 is the file's own default, so the names a build already embeds keep the composed
formulation and the two others take a _v0 and _v1 suffix of their own;
evidence/q4k-scale-decode/ shows each value reproducing its standalone arm's ISA digest bit for
bit at both shapes, which is what makes the multiplexed module the measured one.

The key names the module and the row shape together. NUM_ROWS reaches the shader as
specialization constant 1 and reaches the dispatch as the pipeline's own workgroup denominator,
both from rm_kq in ggml_vk_load_shaders, so a value that moved one alone would dispatch a row
count the shader does not compute; `-rows8` moves both. That suffix is what makes the eight-row
shape reachable at all on this device, since the AMD_GCN branch sets rm_kq = 4 and a decode
therefore never selects the eight-row pipeline.

A value outside v0, v1, v2, and their -rows8 forms ends the load rather than falling back to the
default, since a default served under an arm's name is the confusion the sealed key exists to
remove. The resolved variant and row count reach the log at load, and the census ledger's
spirv_executed_sha256 is the authority on which module the device ran: summarize-bracket-ab.py's
module_identity row already requires one subject digest per role and the two to differ, so a key
that failed to take effect refuses the run without a second mechanism.

Scope: the dense f32_f32 and f16_f32 mat-vec families carry the variants. The MUL_MAT_ID and
q8_1 Q4_K families keep the default formulation under every key, so a MoE checkpoint and an
integer-dot build measure nothing through this key.

